{"seq":37,"t":14.96,"campaign_id":"fixture","body":{"type":"analyst.verdict","hypothesis_id":"h1","verdict":"REFUTED","reasoning":"The predicted correlation is absent, so the hypothesis fails on its own stated criterion. Stability and mobility are separate axes here, which means the search cannot be collapsed — it has to stay multi-objective. Spearman rho = -0.50 across 3 candidates (prediction required > 0.50). The most stable candidate (0.000 eV/atom above hull) has a barrier of 14.66 eV, while the lowest barrier measured is 13.23 eV at 0.014 eV/atom above hull.","evidence":["Spearman rho = -0.50 across 3 candidates (prediction required > 0.50). The most stable candidate (0.000 eV/atom above hull) has a barrier of 14.66 eV, while the lowest barrier measured is 13.23 eV at 0.014 eV/atom above hull."],"heuristics":[{"id":"heu-1","text":"Do not screen Li conductors on stability alone — in the thiophosphates, proximity to the hull does not predict the migration barrier. Score both axes.","learned_from":"h1","strength":"tentative"},{"id":"heu-2","text":"Straight-line hop energies are upper bounds and carry an OOD flag. Treat differences smaller than ~0.1 eV between candidates as noise.","learned_from":"h1","strength":"established"}]}}
