{"seq":44,"t":14.96,"campaign_id":"fixture","body":{"type":"proposal.created","proposal":{"title":"Measure the stability/mobility trade-off directly in Li-P-S","summary":"The screen refuted the idea that stability predicts mobility in this family. The frontier candidates differ on both axes, so the next step is an experiment that measures both on the same pellets.","lead_candidate_ids":["c-mp-985583","c-mp-1097036","c-mp-676361"],"synthesis_route":["Weigh out Li2S, P2S5 and LiCl in the target stoichiometry in an argon glovebox.","Ball-mill 600 rpm, 12 h, ZrO2 media, 10:1 ball-to-powder ratio.","Cold-press at 300 MPa into 10 mm pellets.","Sinter in a sealed quartz ampoule, 550 C for 8 h, then cool at 1 C/min."],"validation_protocol":["XRPD to confirm the target phase and quantify residual precursors.","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy, 25-100 C, to extract total ionic conductivity and the activation energy from an Arrhenius fit.","Li | electrolyte | Li symmetric-cell cycling to find the critical current density and check for dendrite penetration.","Linear sweep voltammetry to locate the real oxidation limit."],"falsification_criteria":["An activation energy from the Arrhenius fit above 0.40 eV refutes the predicted ranking outright.","If the measured activation energies order differently from the computed barriers, the straight-line proxy is not usable for ranking and must be replaced with CI-NEB before any further screening."],"caveats":["MACE-MP-0 reaches a few hundred atoms over picoseconds. It does not predict sintered-pellet microstructure, grain-boundary resistance, or long-term interfacial degradation — and those often decide whether a conductor is usable.","Band gap stands in for the electrochemical window and GGA underestimates it, so the window numbers are conservative and ordinal at best.","Barriers are unrelaxed upper bounds carrying an OOD flag."]}}}
